- op: discuss  # 14a5
  at: '2026-10-30T03:21:52Z'  # 14a5
  by: agent  # 14a5
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 14a5
  clock: 3  # 14a5
  nonce: 14a5  # 14a5
  message: "PREMISE CORRECTION 2026-10-29 (merged dev 408f5950e9), found by the INV-nuzas re-check. The description says the placeholder survives BESIDE the real function the build-target linker resolved. That holds only for a flat layout with the manifest beside the package: the filed repro (pyproject.toml + pkg/cli.py) re-run today still gets both edges, defines_target to python:pkg.cli:0-0:main:external_symbol and calls to the real main. On a src/ layout, and when the script names another package, the linker never finds the file, so there is NO calls edge and the stand-in is the entry's only target. Self-map, hypergumbo survey: packages/hypergumbo-tracker/pyproject.toml lines 55-57 and packages/hypergumbo/pyproject.toml line 60 have only defines_target edges, to the hypergumbo_tracker.cli main / textconv_main and hypergumbo_core.cli main stand-ins; the three real functions have no inbound edge from any manifest. Cause, read in linkers/build_target.py: toml_config stamps target_path as the module path made a file path (hypergumbo_tracker/cli.py), and _resolve_target_path joins it only to the manifest directory, giving packages/hypergumbo-tracker/hypergumbo_tracker/cli.py; the file is packages/hypergumbo-tracker/src/hypergumbo_tracker/cli.py. The meta-package's hypergumbo_core.cli:main lives in packages/hypergumbo-core/src/, which no join of its manifest directory reaches. So the fix has two parts: resolve the dotted target through the python module map (source roots, all workspace packages), then drop or re-point the placeholder. These stand-ins are reached from a production manifest and have an in-tree definition, so they fall outside both INV-nuzas carve-outs. This item now blocks INV-nuzas."  # 14a5
- op: discuss  # 8f61
  at: '2026-10-30T04:47:30Z'  # 8f61
  by: agent  # 8f61
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 8f61
  clock: 4  # 8f61
  nonce: 8f61  # 8f61
  message: "DECISION 2026-10-30 (the owner asked me to investigate how this item reconciles with ADR-0057 and decide; recorded here and on INV-nuzas). THE PLACEHOLDER IS DEMOTED, NOT RE-POINTED OR DELETED; INV-nuzas gains carve-out (c).\nWHY NOT RE-POINT. (1) ADR-0057 is a bound decision (LIVE section 3): a stub is demoted, never deleted, and section 14.1 is this exact case, a pass that CONSUMED a stub naming it in derived_from (build_target already does: derived_from=[src, main, defines_target edge id]). (2) LinkerContext's documented Unresolved Edge Protocol: the analyzer emits the unresolved edge, the linker 'creates proper edge to the resolved symbol'. A rewrite in place would be the second home for one fact. (3) There is no precedent for re-pointing a placeholder: the only dst rewrite in ir/finalize is the external-id canonicaliser.\nWHY THE STUB MAY NOT JUST STAY. ADR-0037 ruling 1: is_resolved=False with a populated identity means an identified EXTERNAL (stdlib / dependency). A placeholder whose module path names an in-tree module and whose function is defined there is no such thing, so the bare stand-in is a false claim, and today the real function gets NO edge at all on a src/ layout or across packages (this item's 10-29 correction).\nWHAT LANDS. (a) build_target resolves a Python target through the manifest dir, its src/, the package-module form (pkg/__init__.py), and else a unique in-tree file with the module's path, refusing an ambiguous one; a Python entry point that names a function no longer falls back to some other main(). (b) build-target-linker gets RegisteredLinker.supersedes_consumed_stub on a measured precision table in docs/audits/ (section 14.1 grants on measurement), so the placeholder is demoted with meta superseded_by naming the in-tree edge: a positive claim io_boundary, taint and backend_agreement already read. (c) INV-nuzas carve-out (c), below.\nNOT ASSERTED: that the demoted stand-in stops being an external_symbol node, or that every consumer counting external nodes reads superseded_by (one that does not over-counts by one per script; that consumer gap is ADR-0057's in general, not this item's, and is a candidate for WI-borib's agreement sweep)."  # 8f61
