- op: discuss  # 3459
  at: '2026-10-30T07:37:14Z'  # 3459
  by: agent  # 3459
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 3459
  clock: 6  # 3459
  nonce: '3459'  # 3459
  message: "Done in PR #1952 (f8180a7ac1). Root cause: build_target looked for a Python console script's module only beside its manifest, so a src/ layout or a script naming another package's module got no calls edge and the placeholder became a workspace-prefixed external_symbol; and a missing named function fell back to some other main(). Fix: the module is looked for in the manifest's src/, as a package (__init__.py), else as the one in-tree file with its path (two name nothing); a named function is taken at its word; build-target-linker holds ADR-0057 section 14.1's supersedes_consumed_stub on docs/audits/0024 (16 of 16 correct over 12 repos), so finalize demotes the placeholder and stamps superseded_by. CLOSURE EVIDENCE on merged dev, production `hypergumbo survey`: (1) the filed repro (pyproject.toml pkgcli = \"pkg.cli:main\" + pkg/cli.py): defines_target -> python:pkg.cli:0-0:main:external_symbol now carries superseded_by = the calls edge's id (edge:sha256:d41471c1571649f2, verified equal) and superseded_by_origin [build-target-linker]; rank_score 0.95 -> 0.475, confidence untouched; calls -> pkg/cli.py main unchanged. (2) The 10-29 correction's case, this repository: all 4 [project.scripts] placeholders (packages/hypergumbo/pyproject.toml:60, packages/hypergumbo-tracker/pyproject.toml:55-57) now have superseded_by naming calls edges to the real hypergumbo_core.cli main, hypergumbo_tracker.cli main and textconv_main, which had no inbound manifest edge before. The stand-in nodes remain (demoted, not deleted, by design); INV-nuzas carve-out (c) covers them, and its self checker now reports them as c:superseded (3 nodes). Not asserted: consumers counting external nodes read superseded_by."  # 3459
